From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Biggart <swbiggart@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:17:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 17/46] flashnext cuda: the decode round graph keys each lane's
 buffers, so a drafted window's verify and keep leave it held

A settle swaps a sequence's DeltaNet state buffers with its window's
spares, and a captured round bakes those addresses in. The round graph's
key now holds each lane's buffer digest (the one the window graphs key on)
and capacity, so a settled lane is a new key, and verify, verifyMany and
rollback no longer clear the graph. launch refuses a pass that carries a
pocket before it captures anything.
